{{- /*
What enrolling a tree writes for Claude Code: the PreToolUse hook that routes a
Bash command through the broker, and the same deny rules `faramir init` writes
into the home.

settings.local.json rather than settings.json: everything here names a path this
machine decided, the binary the hook execs and the directories this install
occupies, and settings.json is the file Claude Code shares with a team. Claude
Code reads both for hooks and permissions, and permission rules merge across
scopes rather than one shadowing the other.

The rules are written here as well as in the home because a tree can be enrolled
on a host where `faramir init --agent claude` never ran, and the enrolment is
what the operator did. Duplication costs nothing: deny rules merge, and a rule
written twice refuses the same thing once.

GENERATED. The paths come from internal/install/protectedpaths.go, written once
and rendered into each agent's own spelling; nothing here is a path of its own.
Add one there.
*/ -}}
{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "{{.BinDir}}/faramir guard",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
{{ jsonLines "      " (claudeRules .Layout) }}
    ]
  }
}
